    <bpmn:process id="W_W1475" name="W1475. Coupon &amp; Promotional Discount Abuse Detection, Pattern Analysis &amp; Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly exception report showing anomalous discount activity; or cashier discount override spike; or loyalty program redemption anomaly
Frequency: Weekly pattern analysis; ~10–20 confirmed abuse cases/month chain-wide
Volume: ~33.6M annual POS transactions; ~6 promotional events/year (per W13) with coupon activity; estimated 0.1–0.3% discount abuse rate
Owner: LP Operations Manager
Participants: LP Analyst, Store Manager, Cashier, Department Supervisor, Marketing (coupon issuance), Loyalty Program Manager
Source: workflow W1475 — Coupon &amp; Promotional Discount Abuse Detection, Pattern Analysis &amp; Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1475_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1475_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1475_Lane2" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1475_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1475_Start4" name="Weekly exception report showing anomalous discount activity; or cashier discount override…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1475_Task5" name="Automated discount exception monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated discount exception monitoring: System continuously monitors POS transactions for discount anomalies: (a) Employee discount misuse: transactions with employee discount applied but customer is not verified employee; (b) Trade discount abuse: trade discount rate applied without trade account scan per W112; (c) Coupon stacking: multiple discount codes applied to single transaction exceeding authorized total discount %; (d) Promo code reuse: same coupon code scanned &gt; stated usage limit per customer; (e) Price override patterns: cashier price overrides &gt; 20% below SRP per W5B requiring manager authorization — frequency by cashier; (f) Loyalty points manipulation: loyalty account with points accumulation spike inconsistent with purchase pattern
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): LP Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1475_Task6" name="Weekly pattern analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly pattern analysis: LP Analyst reviews weekly discount exception report: (a) top 20 cashiers by discount exception rate (discounts applied ÷ total transactions); (b) top 20 stores by promotional discount variance (actual discount % vs. planned discount % per W13 campaign); (c) loyalty accounts with anomalous points activity (earning spikes, rapid redemption, account sharing indicators — multiple phone numbers, multiple store locations); (d) coupon code usage patterns — codes used beyond geographic or time restrictions; (e) LP Analyst categorizes exceptions: systemic (policy gap), individual (single cashier/customer), or organized (coordinated pattern)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1475_Task7" name="Individual case investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Individual case investigation: For flagged exceptions: (a) LP Analyst pulls transaction detail: timestamp, store, terminal, cashier, items, discount type, customer (if loyalty/ trade); (b) review CCTV footage at POS terminal per W838 for visual confirmation (cashier behavior, customer interaction, coupon presentation); (c) interview Cashier and Department Supervisor: was the discount appropriate? was manager authorization obtained? (d) if confirmed abuse: (i) employee — disciplinary action per HR policy (verbal warning for first offense, written warning for second, termination for third), (ii) customer — flag loyalty account, restrict future coupon usage, (iii) coupon code — deactivate and notify Marketing
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1475_Task8" name="Systemic prevention measures">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Systemic prevention measures: LP Analyst recommends preventive controls based on pattern analysis: (a) POS system configuration changes: (i) hard-code coupon exclusions (cannot stack with other discounts), (ii) enforce coupon usage limits per customer (tracked by loyalty account or phone number), (iii) require manager biometric authorization for discounts &gt; 15%; (b) process changes: (i) daily coupon code rotation (codes change daily, texted to registered customers), (ii) trade discount requires trade account card scan (no manual entry), (iii) employee discount restricted to employee&#x27;s own purchases only (verified by employee ID + biometric); (c) Marketing campaign design changes: (i) unique single-use coupon codes instead of generic codes, (ii) digital coupons delivered via app (not printable) to prevent photocopying
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Operations Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1475_Task9" name="Promotional event post-mortem">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Promotional event post-mortem: After each bi-monthly sale event per W13: (a) LP Analyst compiles discount abuse report: total discount exceptions, confirmed abuse cases, financial impact (over-discount amount), policy violations by type; (b) LP Operations Manager reviews with Marketing and Store Operations: (i) were promotional terms clear and enforceable? (ii) did store staff understand discount rules? (iii) what system controls prevented abuse? (iv) what new abuse patterns emerged?; (c) incorporate lessons learned into next promotional event design per W13
Responsible (R): LP Analyst / LP Operations Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1475_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1475_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1475_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1475_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-310 (ensure controlled execution — Exception Monitoring &amp; Investigation (PA-23.1).) | - operational: system controls that close technical loopholes (e.g., coupon stacking restrictions and usage limits)
Owner: LP Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1475_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1475_Annotation11" targetRef="W1475_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow13" sourceRef="W1475_Start4" targetRef="W1475_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow14" sourceRef="W1475_Task5" targetRef="W1475_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow15" sourceRef="W1475_Task6" targetRef="W1475_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow16" sourceRef="W1475_Task7" targetRef="W1475_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow17" sourceRef="W1475_Task8" targetRef="W1475_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1475_Flow18" sourceRef="W1475_Task9" targetRef="W1475_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1475_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1475_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1475">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1475_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1475_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
