    <bpmn:process id="W_W1542" name="W1542. Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Pattern Detection, Multi-Store Correlation &amp; Law Enforcement Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Exception-based reporting (EBR) system identifies pattern of related theft incidents across multiple stores; or LP Officer reports suspected organized ring
Frequency: ~5–10 suspected ORC investigations/year; ongoing monitoring
Volume: Each investigation may involve 3–10 stores and PHP 500K–5M in losses
Owner: LP Director
Participants: LP Director, Regional LP Officers, Store Managers, IT Security, Legal Counsel, Philippine National Police (PNP)
Source: workflow W1542 — Organized Retail Crime (ORC) Pattern Detection, Multi-Store Correlation &amp; Law Enforcement Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1542_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1542_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1542_Lane2" name="LP Director">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1542_Lane3" name="Regional LP Officers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1542_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1542_Start5" name="Exception-based reporting (EBR) system identifies pattern of related theft incidents…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1542_Task6" name="Pattern detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pattern detection: System analyzes loss patterns across all 200 stores — (a) same SKU category with unusual shrinkage spikes at ≥ 3 stores within 30 days, (b) same vehicle/license plate at multiple store loading zones, (c) similar suspicious transaction patterns (excessive returns without receipt, repeated high-value voids by same cashier), (d) CCTV correlation of same individuals at multiple stores; generates ORC alert with supporting data
Responsible (R): System / Regional LP Officer
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: Automated + 2 hours/review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task7" name="Investigation activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Investigation activation: LP Director reviews ORC alert; classifies investigation priority — High (losses &gt; PHP 1M or suspected internal collusion), Medium (PHP 200K–1M), Low (&lt; PHP 200K); assigns lead investigator; creates confidential investigation file restricted from store-level access
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task8" name="Multi-store evidence gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Multi-store evidence gathering: Regional LP Officers at affected stores pull CCTV footage, transaction logs, exception reports, and inventory variance data; IT Security extracts digital evidence (access logs, transaction timestamps, POS override records); all evidence consolidated in secure investigation file
Responsible (R): Regional LP Officers / IT Security
Accountable (A): LP Director
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task9" name="Suspect identification &amp; surveillance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Suspect identification &amp; surveillance: For High-priority investigations, LP Director authorizes enhanced surveillance at targeted stores — additional CCTV monitoring, undercover LP presence, vehicle tracking (if warranted and legally permissible); coordinates with store management to maintain normal operations during surveillance
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task10" name="Law enforcement coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Law enforcement coordination: For confirmed ORC cases with sufficient evidence, LP Director coordinates with PNP Criminal Investigation Division — submits formal complaint with evidence dossier (CCTV footage, transaction records, inventory reports); Legal Counsel reviews to ensure BuildRight&#x27;s reporting obligations are met and employee rights are protected
Responsible (R): LP Director / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 8–16 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task11" name="Internal collusion investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Internal collusion investigation (if applicable): If evidence suggests employee involvement (e.g., cashier processing fraudulent voids, receiving clerk facilitating theft), LP Director coordinates with HR for employee investigation per W79 (grievance process); ensures due process while maintaining investigation integrity; employee suspension pending investigation per DOLE requirements
Responsible (R): LP Director / HR Head
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1542_Task12" name="Case closure &amp; prevention measures">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Case closure &amp; prevention measures: Upon case resolution (arrest, recovery, or closure), LP Director documents lessons learned; implements targeted prevention measures — enhanced CCTV angles at affected areas, POS procedure changes, vendor collaboration for product tagging; updates ORC pattern library in EBR system for future detection improvement
Responsible (R): LP Director
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4 hours/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1542_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1542_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1542_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1542_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-310 (ensure controlled execution — Exception Monitoring &amp; Investigation (PA-23.1).) | - operational: LP Director review and approval gate
Owner: LP Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
